  "prefLabel": "Saf-C 1401.36 Physical operator",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Saf-C 1401.36 “Physical operator” means the person who physically controls the operation of a carnival or amusement ride while said carnival or amusement ride is being used by, or is open to, the public.\n\nSource. #2229, eff 12-31-82; ss by #2950, eff 1-3-85; ss by #4531, eff 1-1-89; ss by #5940, INTERIM, eff 1-1-95; ss by #5952, eff 1-24-95, EXPIRED: 1-24-03\n\nNew. #7833, INTERIM, eff 2-22-03, EXPIRED: 8-21-03\n\nNew. #8045, eff 2-20-04; ss by #8342, eff 4-28-05, EXPIRED: 1-2-14 (see Revision Note #2 at chapter heading for Saf-C 1400)\n\nNew. #10507, eff 1-21-14; renumbered by #13535, INTERIM (formerly Saf-C 1401.27); EXPIRED: 1-21-24\n\nNew. #13984, EMERGENCY RULE, eff 5-24-24, EXPIRED: 11-20-24\n\nNew. #14139, eff 11-28-24, EXPIRES: 11-28-34 (formerly Saf-C 1401.32)",
